Mustafa’s Story | Newcastle, NSW | 08 July 2026 
mosaicmc.org.au 
 
 
It  was  through  COMPACT  that  Sami  connected  him  to  Joseph Wright,  one  of  the 
better-known coaches around Newcastle, who  ran a training program for local kids. 
Joe met him and asked him to help coach. 
He said no. 
Here was a man who had played for his country's youth teams and carried a coaching 
licence from home, and when he was asked to stand in front of a group of Australian 
children, he did not  believe he was good enough. "In the coaching  there is a lot of 
responsibilities," he says. "You have to deliver the messages, the plan. I feel at that time 
I was not ready." 
So, he did not coach. He played. 
 
Mustafa playing for the Stockton Sharks FC Vs Newcastle Suns FC, 18/07/2025, Myers Park 
 
Through COMPACT he was introduced to Newcastle Olympic, and he played two full 
seasons.  Then  to  Stockton  Sharks,  where  he  lined  up  in  first  grade.  Two  years  back 
inside the game, watching other coaches, listening to other players, saying little. 
And then one day he decided he was ready. 

 
